        <profile name="Scouts" id="abf4-d641-7381-735b" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">The unit gains the Scouts X" ability, X being its rating.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Deadly Demise" id="49ae-2b3a-58bc-903c" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">When this model is destroyed, after the units embarked within it have made their emergency disembark moves:
  -&gt; Roll one D6: on a 6+, for each unit: while the unit is within 6" of this model, the unit suffers a number of mortal wounds equal to its rating.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Damaged" id="8b15-319b-249b-3a77" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">While the model has X or fewer wounds remaining, X being its rating, this model gets -1 to Hit rolls.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Forward Assault Warsuit" id="63fc-f3cc-ff6a-977a" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">-&gt; At the start of the battle round, if during the first battle round, you can:
  -&gt; Select one enemy unit, binding it as mark selection (your Mark target). When your Mark target is destroyed, you must select one enemy unit, binding it as mark selection to replace it. Only one such designation can be active for this bearer unit. For the rest of the battle, each time a model in this unit makes an attack against it, while the unit is tagged mark, you can re-roll a Wound roll of 1.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
