      <profiles>
        <profile name="Headhunters" id="6330-47ef-ecdc-6429" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">-&gt; At the start of the battle round, if during the first battle round, you can:
  -&gt; Select up to one enemy unit, binding it as quarry selection (your Quarry target). When your Quarry target is destroyed, you must select up to one enemy unit, binding it as quarry selection to replace it. Only one such designation can be active for this bearer unit. For the rest of the battle, each time a model in this unit makes an attack against it, while the target is tagged quarry, the unit's weapons gain [DEVASTATING WOUNDS] and [PRECISION].</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Let Loose the Wolves" id="9bbd-1de4-33c7-cc35" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">When declaring Battle Formations, you may use this ability, split the unit into one unit of each of its WOLF GUARD HEADTAKER and HUNTING WOLVES models.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Hunting Hounds" id="7b4a-0aaf-06b5-4a97" hidden="false" typeId="9cc3-6d83-4dd3-9b64" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="9b8f-694b-e5e-b573">While the unit is not Battle-shocked, while the unit is within 6" of a friendly SPACE WOLVES CHARACTER model (excluding WULFEN models), until the end of the battle round, set the unit's Objective Control characteristic to 1.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
