  </sharedSelectionEntryGroups>
  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Combat Doctrines" id="b872-9bc1-1978-41ae" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of your Command phase, you may use this ability, until the start of your next Command phase:
  -&gt; Select one (each may be chosen once per battle):
    - Assault Doctrine: when the unit is selected to make an Advance move: the unit is eligible to declare a charge even if it Advanced this turn.
    - Devastator Doctrine: ranged weapons equipped by models in this unit gain [ASSAULT].
    - Tactical Doctrine: when the unit is selected to make a Fall Back move: the unit is eligible to shoot even if it Fell Back this turn; the unit is eligible to declare a charge even if it Fell Back this turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Transhuman Strategist" id="2deb-4d9b-912f-5201" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the battle round, while this model has the Transhuman Strategist ability, while this model is the Warlord, you gain 1CP.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Librarius" id="b432-323e-5c73-aadd" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of the battle round, all friendly ADEPTUS ASTARTES PSYKER units' psychic level becomes their Psyker Level characteristic.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Special Move Types" id="cdce-9c0c-5458-108c" hidden="false">
      <description>Shock Disembark Move (the Shock mode of a Disembark move):
  - A unit can make this move only if the unit is embarked and the Transport this unit is embarked within is on the battlefield and the unit did not embark this phase.
  - After it moves, until the end of the turn: the unit cannot declare a charge.
Assault Disembark move (the Assault mode of a Disembark move):
  - Each model is set up wholly within 3" of that Transport.
  - A unit can make this move only if the unit is embarked and the Transport this unit is embarked within is on the battlefield and the unit did not embark this phase and not (the Transport this unit is embarked within advanced this phase or the Transport this unit is embarked within fell back this phase).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Combat Doctrines" id="7709-3249-b5b8-1bdf" hidden="false">
      <description>At the start of your Command phase, you may use this ability, until the start of your next Command phase:
  -&gt; Select one (each may be chosen once per battle):
